A||||17||Shaun41178||Ran my new best A 14.4 ET.
Z||000000||Shaun41178||08-13-99||01:48 AM||||I went to Norwalk last night(wed) and ran an allnew best time for me.  A 14.4 at a measly 89 mph.  The mph sucks for a 14.4 but I don't care cause it is still a 14.4<p>My mods include a K&N intake of my own design, ported stock exhasut manifolds, underdrive pulley, Crane Ignition, Accel wires, and a 70 hp shot of Nitrous Oxide baby.  Thats right the big blue bottle.  <p>My best before this time was a 14.8 at 91.  The difference this time was that I disconnected the torque converter pulg on the bellhousing, installed a power pulley, and iced the intake good before the run.<p>i just thoought some of you might want to know.  Next planned mod is a shift kit and a 2.5 inch cat back exhaust.  I hope to run a 14.3 or if I am lucky a 14.2 after these mods are done.  Then perhaps going to 1.6 rockers and see what that does.<p>Well i just thought i would let the forum know.  Good day to all.
Z||000001||Pretender||08-13-99||03:49 AM||||About that shift kit, what "brand" ar you thinking about using?. i asked on the tech. forum and no one replied. i think the secret to the 14's & 13's would be the auto tranny up grade. i would also like to install a higher gear ratio for the 1/4 mile maybe a 3.73? any opinions on that?..is it even poss.? did you also run with out the funny gas?. get a pr(personal record) at that? what was your reaction time for your best run?..int he 5's. when i ran the 16.2 it was a 6 something but it got me a bi in the next round becuase it was the best on that round. All i got was a stupid trophey for 3rd place. i paid $20 to race. 
Z||000002||lowCG||08-13-99||05:18 AM||||What kind of stall converters are available for the auto cars?<br>I heard of a Vega unit,beefed up for smallblock use going for $70,raises stall to around 1800-2000 RPM in V8 cars.<br>How about a Chevette,or maybe a TH125, Fiat/Opel/U.S.postal truck  converter?
Z||000003||Cooter||08-13-99||04:46 PM||||Back in my hot rod days, I found that a stock Vega converter in a mild small block car stalled at about 2500 rpms. The same converter stalled at about 4000 behind my big block 402. With this size/style converter, the more torque, the higher the stall speed. So. .  . if that is still true, a stock 4 cyl converter should have a higher stall in the v6 car. Maybe someone with a lot of time can check this out to be sure. I think it would be worth checking into because it is a factory piece and costs should be reasonible.
Z||000004||batboy||08-13-99||05:57 PM||||Shaun, those are excellent 1/4 mile times for a Fiero. I was thinking, dang, that almost faster than my V8 will probably be, then I remember you are using that blue bottled gas. Maybe I ought to hit my 350 with some juice?<p>About those torque converters (T/C). We used to use power glide T/C's in turbo 350 trannies for higher stall speeds and turbo 350 T/C's in turbo 400 trannies for higher stall speeds. However, I don't know how that might relate to the TH 125 transmission used in Fieros.<p>You need to find a smaller T/C that will bolt to the flexplate and will fit into the transmission too. Generally, the smaller the T/C, the higher the stall speed.
Z||000005||Shaun41178||08-14-99||03:08 AM||||Pretender:  I have purchased the shift kit from the Fiero Store.  It is a green box and it says Mr. Shift on it.  I have never heard of Mr.shift before but on the box it also says Transgo.  So i am guessing it is made by Transgo but marketed under Mr. Shift.  It has yet to be installed.  I don't know how well it will work or if I will like it but we will soon find out.<p>I have purchased a 3.33 tranny from an 86 Gt.  This is higher then my 3.06 stock so I am guessing that with this tranny and the shift kit in it I will be able to cut .2 in the qtr and gain a few mph as well.  I do not know if custom gears for the Final drive can be cut like a 3.73 or if they are even available.<p>Sorry but I did not make a NA run.  I only ran on the nitrous that night.  My 60' for my 14.4 run was a 1.95 and my reaction time was .745.  yea that sucks and need to work on that but only way to do that is to hit the track more and learn how long it takes for my car to react after punching the throttle.<p>i paid $7 to run that night
Z||000006||Pretender||08-15-99||01:16 AM||||it does take practice and they say that practice makes perfect!, so for i have logged in 47 runs at our local track and 90% of the time i can cut a 5 something light unless i'm in that damned right lane!..for some reason sitting in my car looking to the left is alot harder for me to hit the gas for some reason, why?, i have no idea it could be all in my head. When you get that shift kit installed be sure to tell us all about it, that and the ing. is my next mod, and the plan is N20 before sept. 25(the last street night here) i can't wait to see the older guys faces when i bust off a 14!...i'll have to run in the modified class but i'm locating the bottle in the front(will i have to buy more line?, anything else?) and trying like heck to hide everything!. When i went to the Englishtown Import vs. American race(New Jersey) they didn't even look anywhere 'cept for the battery. and even then i find it to be funny because they automatically go to the front of the car, morons. How hard was it to install your ing.? When the gas kicks in does it make a distinct sound? i don't want anybody to know what i got, sorry about all the q's but your the only one that more or less has the same plans about these auto's. thanks...shawn.
Z||000007||terryk||08-15-99||03:25 PM||||"I think the secret to the 14's & 13's would be the auto tranny up grade. i would also like to install a higher gear ratio for the 1/4 mile maybe a 3.73? any opinions on that?..is it even poss.? " <p>Look in the wrecking yards for 1983 X-11 Automatics. There were a number of them built with 3:56 final drive. I have one. Dang thing turns 3000 at 60MPH with the converter locked. The trans code is 3CD. I figured this out by calling GM and having them look it up.<p>Keep in mind, it's annoying to cruise.
Z||000008||Pretender||08-15-99||04:53 PM||||that sounds like the anwser to my question!, but may i ask what kind of car is the X-11 tranny in? and does it just "drop"(no mods?) right in?
Z||000009||Pretender||08-15-99||05:18 PM||||my brain is in the clouds todaym, do you mean the auto tranny from the 84's. how does one tell the difference?..the number you mentioned is it marked any where else on the car?., the cars at the boneyard are all on the ground!..those bastards!., thek killed 2M4!
Z||000010||batboy||08-15-99||05:28 PM||||The Chevy X-11 was the sporty, hi-po version of the Citation. A guy I worked with bought a new one in the early 80's, it was pretty quick for a Citation.
Z||000011||terryk||08-16-99||09:01 AM||||1983 Citation X-11 Automatic with THM125C transmission. 3CD is on a paper label glued to the side cover. 3 means "1983". I've never seen a 2CD or 4CD, or 5CD. 81's didn't have TCC.
Z||000012||Shaun41178||08-18-99||02:59 AM||||Pretender:  The nitrous kit that I bought came with a 14 fott nitrous line.  That shouold be more then enough to mount the bottle in the front and run the line to the back of the car.<p>The ignition was very easy to install.  The directions for the Crane HI-6 with PS-91 Coil were easy to follow and nothing had to be cut or spliced that was factory cause a special plug came with the kit to plug into the stock components.  I like this casue if the box fails I can simply and quickly go back to the stock ignition system.<p>When hitting the nitrous, there is no distinct sound coming from the engine.  No one will know you have it unless you tell them or show them.  I do however have a hissing noise coming from my engien compartment because I have my own intake setup going and have no air silencer so a very distinct sucking sound can be heard.<p>Good luck finding an old X-11.  I have never seen one here in NW Ohio.  You could probably go to a yard if they have a computer system it is probably linked to other j-yards with computers and they list inventories so it is possible that a j-yard in another state can get you the tranny you want.  Good luck with that though if you are going to go through with it.
Z||000013||DXR_WILL||08-19-99||01:48 PM||||Shaun41178<br>I like the performance mods you have done to your Fiero.  I was wondering if you think the mods you did to your Fiero are worth the money?  I'm asking because I want to buy performance parts for my dad's Fiero and all the performance parts for the Fiero are expensive.  For the price of a cat back exhaust system you can get a NOS kit.  Yours and anybody's input would be greatly respected.
Z||000014||Shaun41178||08-20-99||01:06 AM||||DXR Will:  The mods I have done to my engine in my opinion are way worth it.  But if I was to be limited to only being able to keep one mod, it would be the nitrous.  All the others can go.  The nitrous made the biggest difference in the acceleration and qtr mile time improvements then any other mod.  I was running low 16's before the nitrous and other mods and I am now running mid 14's.  This is only with the nitrous, underdrive pulley, crane ignition, ported exhasut manifolds and the custom K&N with cone filter.  I do not know what I run without the nitrous now as i have yet to do any n/a runs for a long time.<p>I would have to say that if you can not afford the nitrous then go with an underdrive pulley and ported stock exhaust manifolds.  I went from a 14.8 to a 14.4 with the pulley and a few other tricks like icing the intake.  So I can safely say that the underdrive pulley took off .1 in the qtr mile and perhaps even .2 with the nitrous.  N/a I am unsure how much it will help.  The ported exhasut manifolds added 8 hp to my car as I had it dynoed.  Your car will probably vary but will be around 8<p>I plan on having a cat-back put on my car as well.  However it will be of my own design pretty much.  Actually it will be a 2.5 inch system with a flowmaster muffler and finished off with Borla tips.  The whole conversion will cost around $250 or so and without the tips will be around $180-$190.  I expect to lose low end torque when n/a but gain a few hp on the top end in n/a.  With the nitrous I expect to gain about 10 hp over the stock system just cause of the extra oxygen being injected into the engine it needs a bigger exhasut to expedite the exhaust faster and more free.  I am having this done at a muffler shop.  I am also going to install a high flow cat.<p>I have been very satisfied with all the mods I have made to my car and feel that they are all worth it for my particular application.  The only reason I got the ignition was because I was running nitrous.  If not running a high hp engien or one that is mostly stock then the factory ignition will do just fine.<p>Any more questions I will try to answer/help as best as I can.<p>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178
Z||000015||Pretender||08-22-99||04:46 AM||||thats great!., i thought the N20 would make a distinctive sound!., i can modifty it without anyone knowing about it!., the major races that my friends attend have to go through  a major "tech!"., i was watching and they never checked the rear engined rear drive cars(nsx's,mr2's,fiero's.Delorians,etc." . there is a race on oct. 10 i think!., i'll look at it  tomorrow for the list..L8r..<IMG SRC="/ubb/redface.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15>)1
Z||000016||DXR_WILL||08-22-99||07:02 PM||||Shaun<br>have you thought about adding more NOS?  I'm pretty shure the Fiero can handle more then a 70 shot system.
Z||000017||batboy||08-23-99||01:59 AM||||I'm not sure I'd go higher than a 50 shot unless you're running good forged pistons. A well prepped 2.8/3.1 ought to handle a 70 shot. Anymore than that and you're asking for trouble, nitrous is incredibly hard on engines. When you kick in the gas, cylinder pressure is unbelieveable. If there is a weak point in your engine, it will find it and destroy it. Go easy on the nitrous at first.
